        summary:
          'Stanford\'s August 2026 revision of its ADP payroll study found that employment among workers aged 22 to 25 in AI-exposed occupations sits 19% below where it would be had it kept pace with less exposed peers, and that the adjustment operates through reduced hiring rather than layoffs. The number is not the point: the mechanism is. Young employment falls where knowledge is codified and rises, for experienced workers, where it is tacit. This piece argues that tacit knowledge gets manufactured by passing through the codified kind, and that the mechanical work AI absorbed was also the only curriculum we had. With the LSE counterargument included and five concrete decisions for whoever runs an area or signs a contract.',
